{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1395335-companion-theocentrism-evidance-dials","id":1395335,"title":"[Companion] Theocentrism & Evidance Dials","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-06-09T06:54:40-07:00","id":1395335,"title":"[Companion] Theocentrism & Evidance Dials","content":"So <b>Scion 2E Companion - Mysteries of the World</b> is for backers and in errata, right now. It will be published in coming weeks/months. But we know about one of it's main features - Myth Levels / Dials. They are sum up of each chronicles setting changes, loosely connected to <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ages_of_Man\" target=\"_blank\">Hesoid's Ages of Man</a>, that point changes in World setting that they reflects. <b>How would you run your World setting, if you went outside of basis of it? What repercussion each Dial can have on the World?</b><br /> <br /> For vanilla setting of World ( main gameline settings ) are those:<ul><li>Genre : Bronze</li> <li>Theocentrism : Gold</li> <li>Titanomachy : Silver</li> <li>Evidence : Silver</li> </ul><br /> Full <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/mysteries-of-the-world-scion-2e/\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Myth Levels Blog post</b></a> that sumed-up this idea in long developing process before, 1,5 year ago. Here is spoilers sum-up:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Myth Levels preview</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <b>CHAPTER ONE: MYTH LEVEL</b><br /> <br /> The Myth Level is five options along four axes of design, meant to allow the Storyguide to choose how many of Scion\u2019s setting \u201cdials\u201d they want to crank. This chapter lays out what each of those dials looks like at each of the five Myth Levels. Those Myth Levels are:<ul><li><b>Iron:</b> Perfectly mundane. Very similar in nature and tone to Gaiman\u2019s <b><i>American Gods</i></b>, where ifriti are cab drivers, Odhinn is a shiftless wandering con man, and Chernobog and the goddesses of dawn, midday and evening are poor immigrants scraping by in a shitty apartment in Chicago.</li> <li><b>Heroic: </b>Mostly mundane, but with room for great acts of heroism. Most supernatural creatures still have mundane manifestations here (that centaur is still just a biker here), but Scions and gods may appear as impressive and tremendous \u2013 Aphrodite isn\u2019t some burnt out barfly here, she\u2019s drop-dead gorgeous and probably on fashion covers. This is the level of the <b><i>Iliad</i> </b>and the <i><b>Odyssey</b></i>.</li> <li><b>Bronze: </b>This is where the supernatural really comes into play. Creatures of Legend shed their mundane disguises in areas of Bronze Myth, and appear in their true nature. Magic becomes overt here, and Demigods wield their true power. This is <b><i>Clash of the Titans</i></b> territory, and there might just actually be dragons in that undetailed area of the map.</li> <li><b>Silver: </b>Past the threshold of urban myth and getting into epic fantasy, places of Silver Myth are deeply resonant with Myth. They are often fanciful places and hidden vales of magic technically found in the World, but not of it. The power of a creature of Legend is reflected in its appearance \u2013 the mightier the entity, the more impressive it appears. Zelazny\u2019s <i><b>Lord of Light</b> </i>goes into this area of Myth in its narrative.</li> <li><b>Gold:</b> Flat-out mythological, where symbolism is the same as its reality. Places of Gold Myth are not even of this World. Lots of <b>Scion</b> 1e went into this territory, with its otherworldly locales, and lots of fantasy that touches on extradimensional areas and the like qualify.</li> </ul>The trick is this: you should be able to choose a starting Myth Level and then turn each dial up or down within that level to taste. So, for instance, as Storyguide I might choose to start at the Iron Level but crank the Titanomachy up, turning <b><i>American Gods</i></b> into a raging shadow war that you have to keep peeling back layers of the World to see.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-09T06:59:19-07:00","id":1395336,"title":"","content":"Here are my personal takes - I prefer the <b>Scion </b>setting where claims of Pantheons are not whole truth and <i>'All Myths are True' </i>tagline is resolved by 'Oh, they SAY that - and the gods have real magic - but Earth still has 4.54 billion years and dinosaurs where real before - just like evolution'. I'm also very low on Evidence, really like to run games like <b>American Gods </b>( in examples above ) or <b>World/Chronicles of Darkness</b>. Both are connected to my pre-Myth Levels concept idea of <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1275725-2e-setting-hack-gods-in-hiding-and-new-mythic-age\">Gods Are In Hiding</a> Hack.<br /> <br /> Example game I have in my mind would probably be something like that:<br /> <i>'Story about simple people slowly introduced to world of Gods and Heroes. At least major religion and Myths are true, even when Earth has more or less stable history to this point. Titans where secret threat for centuries - now, with Global Warming, new Titan War will restart. However, all of that is outside of normal people do not - cannot - see it all. Oh, and Atlantis is returning on Earth...'</i><br /> <br /> So this chronicle would like:<br /> <b>Genre Iron ( Near Min ) -&gt; Bronze</b> - Generally casual plots with 'some myths were beside it' and uncovering world of Gods - until players go to Hero Tier and start to be involved in new Titan War<br /> <b>Theocentrism Bronze ( Middle )</b> - All major Pantheons of corebooks exists. Rest is not sure / only on story needs. Earth has still stable history of existing 4.54 billion years. Maybe as a result of first Titanomachy we have this 'reality consensus', not sure on that.<br /> <b>Titanomachy Iron ( Min ) -&gt; Silver</b> - It would mean that starting status quo is 'Secret Cold War with Titans' that in time of Hero Tier goes to almost open conflict with them.<br /> <b>Evidance Iron ( Min ) </b>- Gods and Pantheons are secret to population at large, separated from them by Mythic Mists ( my mechanics hack before Companion rules, from Gods in Hiding topic ).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 06-09-2020, 10:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-09T09:08:05-07:00","id":1395359,"title":"","content":"Okay you got a good number of those wrong, especially the Theocentrism.Theocentrism isn't a measure of &quot;Yeah but how much of what the Gods say is lies?&quot; it's &quot;How much favortism does one Pantheon get over the others?&quot;<br /> <br /> So if you have Theocentrism Iron favoring the Aesir, that means that the Aesir are the 'Right' Pantheon, and in fact may be the only ones that exist. So even if you have Theocentrism down to the lowest setting, <i>that Aesir-focused world is still gonna be Midgard wrapped in the branches of the World Tree</i>.<br /> <br /> Also, in the default Scion setting, the World IS a hunk of rock that's been around for several billion years. AND a turtle that floats through space. AND was created by any number of Pantheons. It's all true, all of it. Maybe some from a Certain Point of View, but it's All True.<br /> <br /> Edit: [Section removed for being kind of a jackass statement]","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":2142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","user":"Kyman201","date":". 06-09-2020, 08:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-09T09:46:15-07:00","id":1395378,"title":"","content":"As I understand it on reading the preview:<br /> <br /> <b>Genre </b>is more about the flashiness or the physicality, so if I get the read of your setting right, Wyrd, you're looking at Heroic, mostly the investigation and mystery of uncovering the divine, with some combat sprinkled in, Bronze if it's a more even mix.<br /> <b>Theocentrism</b>, as Kyman explained, is more about pantheon priorities. So if you have all of them in equal measure, even if subdued as yours seem to be, you're right up in Gold<br /> <b>Titanomachy </b>is how relevent Titans are to the World, how important an enemy they are. You're probably starting at Bronze, in fact Companion specifically mentions Titans at Bronze engage in a cold war with the Gods.<br /> <b>Evidence</b>, I'd say you have the right of it. Magic and the like at Iron is a well kept secret, though you might go up to Bronze if you have larger secret societies and whatnot knowing about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26056,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26056-cassiecataria","user":"CassieCataria","date":".  Spelling 06-09-2020, 12:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26056-cassiecataria","name":"CassieCataria","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26056_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-09T10:01:01-07:00","id":1395382,"title":"","content":"Yeah, what Cassie said. From what you've described of your preferred game tone, I think Cassie has the right of it with your preferred Settings.<br /> <br /> So Theocentrism will be Gold since you're assuming all of them are on equal footing, while the Genre and Evidence are cranked down to Iron at the start.<br /> <br /> The Companion even has rules for some of these: For instance, Iron Genre puts a limit on how flashy the Stunts you pick can be, and makes it so that Marvels and Boons used in Non-Procedural parts are more expensive, while the Evidence section includes a special Condition for lower-rank Evidence settings where you've strained the Disbelief too much and now You're In Trouble until you help cover it up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-09T14:37:03-07:00","id":1395461,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1395335-companion-theocentrism-evidance-dials?p=1395359#post1395359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Look I know you're not a massive fan of the All Myths Are True premise and the Setting Dials are a fun idea but if you don't have the companion you don't need to make another pointless thread about your pointless game changes when you haven't even seemed to read the book or mechanics in question. It's fine to not know some things, and it's fine if you haven't read the Companion because it was too late to back the kickstarter when you heard about the game, but you don't need to get on a podium to advertise that you don't know anything but you're going to assume anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Your tone needs adjustment. It's not your place to regulate other gamers' habits.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-09T17:37:04-07:00","id":1395485,"title":"","content":"You're right, sorry, that was out of line.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-14T08:03:51-07:00","id":1396385,"title":"","content":"Hmm. I feel like I want to try a &quot;Scion as Changeling the Dreaming&quot; type setting, with Genre and Evidence somewhere between Iron and Heroic, Theocentrism at Gold, and Titanomachy as somewhere between Heroic and Bronze, maybe. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-14T09:20:12-07:00","id":1396405,"title":"","content":"The Setting Dials idea sounds really cool, but imma wait till I read Mysteries of the World before I get involved in the discussion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-17T18:56:53-07:00","id":1397190,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1395335-companion-theocentrism-evidance-dials?p=1395359#post1395359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay you got a good number of those wrong, especially the Theocentrism.Theocentrism isn't a measure of &quot;Yeah but how much of what the Gods say is lies?&quot; it's &quot;How much favortism does one Pantheon get over the others?&quot;<br /> <br /> So if you have Theocentrism Iron favoring the Aesir, that means that the Aesir are the 'Right' Pantheon, and in fact may be the only ones that exist. So even if you have Theocentrism down to the lowest setting, <i>that Aesir-focused world is still gonna be Midgard wrapped in the branches of the World Tree</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>From what I read in preview, you are mostly right - <i>however</i>, there are also points to Theocentrism as impact of Gods on the World.<br /> <br /> Theocentrism at large:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Companion 2E, p. 12</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Supernatural Presence:</b> It\u2019s also possible to use this axis to dial the prominence of divinity at large up and down. Establishing that every pantheon is non-dominant in The World makes for an underdog or comeback story for Scions and other supernatural beings. This affects how strong an influence Fate has on mortals and how much characters struggle to access their divine powers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Iron Theocentrism:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Companion 2E, p. 12</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">If <i>no</i> pantheons or Gods are important, divinity at large is completely down and out, struggling just to survive in a world where humanity has lost its faith. Godly Incarnations scrape and beg for scraps of influence and Scions are their last-ditch effort to restore their own relevance.</div> </div> </div> </div>Heroic Theocentrism:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Companion 2E, p. 13</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">If <i>no</i> pantheon dominates, divine elements are present and well-known but weak or diluted, rarely making an appearance unless they have something important to accomplish; it takes frequent public miracles to convince mortals the Gods aren\u2019t on their way out for good.<br /> Heroic monotheism includes peripheral or apocryphal myths as part of its core cosmology by default, such as the ifrit of Islam and the Abrahamic Nephilim; mythic personages may be interpreted as Mantles of or transplants from other pantheons (this is, in fact, how Lilith ended up a Liminal figure within Abrahamic myth in our own world despite her roots as a demon in Sumerian mythology).</div> </div> </div> </div>Bronze Theocentrsim:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Companion 2E, p. 13</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">If <i>no</i> pantheon dominates, the divine still fights an uphill battle, but the tide is turning in its favor and the supernatural bleeds through into The World more often. Mortals actively quest to restore it and Scions more closely resemble the larger-than-life Heroes the default World knows.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-17T19:02:53-07:00","id":1397192,"title":"","content":"The more I read the rules, the more I came to idea that I describe general Heroic level Myths. Each combination of Dials has sum up of how the chronicle will look like on this level...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>EVERYDAY PROWESS: THE HEROIC SERIES</b><br /> Characters in a consonant Heroic story live in a World that is decidedly magical, but the magic is hard to find. They meet creatures of Legend who are more or less open about their natures as a matter of course, though such creatures completely human and divine powers usually wear a disguise of exceptional skill or absurd luck. The Heroic World is pulpier, the characters are a bit larger than life, but ordinary mortals mostly don\u2019t notice unless they get dragged into things via Fatebinding. They acknowledge faiths other than their own but still don\u2019t pay them much mind. Like Denizens, titanspawn are more common, lurking around playing espionage games and scouting out the major players, but the Titanomachy is still cold and many Hero-tier Scions don\u2019t realize it\u2019s coming except in the occasional vague omen. Good inspirations for the consonant Heroic Homer\u2019s Iliad and and Odyssey </div> </div> </div>I would simply use the <b>American God</b>'s from later chapters or TV seasons as example for that, but <b>Iliad </b>and <b>Odyssey</b> also works. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-17T19:13:59-07:00","id":1397197,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Please don't post chunks of a book that hasn't been released.<br /> <br /> Describe the text if you want but don't share it.<br /> <br /> This is an official warning.</span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-17T20:36:41-07:00","id":1397215,"title":"","content":"Quoting copyrighted text aside I admit I missed those parts, possibly because when I crack open a book about playing as Heroes and Champions of Gods my exact last impulse is &quot;Okay how do I actively get rid of or neuter Gods in this setting?&quot;<br /> <br /> Like it'd be like getting the rules for any given World of Darkness game... And then going &quot;Also vampires, werewolves, changelings, Mages, none of them exist. They don't make any logical sense, so I'm removing all of them&quot;<br /> <br /> Like, you CAN, but if you reduce the vampires in any given Vampire game to &quot;There's only like six of them and they kinda suck&quot; like... <i>Why bother playing Vampire</i>?<br /> <br /> (American Gods was okay when I read it but I'm not going to read it again, TBH)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-18T05:57:40-07:00","id":1397277,"title":"","content":"I'll note that the no-longer-quoted text starts with a disclaimer for Iron Theocentrism that \u201c<i>if</i> there isn't a particular Pantheon that's being featured, <i>then</i> this setting represents a case where the gods are almost completely shut out from the World, and the nature of the World is predominantly atheistic.\u201d the counterpoint to that is that if there <i>is</i> a particular Pantheon that's dominant, then the World conforms to their cosmology. I, too, don't see much point in this particular arrangement; and I doubt I'll lever use this version of the lowest setting for Theocentrism. To me, it's more of a special case than it is \u201cwhat minimal Theocentrism means\u201d. And it feels more like the sort of thing you'd get when you turn the Evidence dial all the way down.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 07-30-2020, 07:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-18T07:02:22-07:00","id":1397280,"title":"","content":"I have to say, I agree - why play a game about Scions and their divine parents, and then find every way possible to remove the fantastic from the game? It seems self-defeating.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","name":"Purple Snit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5627_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"309"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-18T07:28:07-07:00","id":1397283,"title":"","content":"I must agree with wyrd. If my game runs around a world mundane in general with pontual magic, or a game where the gods struggle with the lack of faith, Iron/Heroic Theocentrism is the way.<br /> <br /> I honestly don\u2019t see any fun on a game where your character is no more than a peon in a game of ancient Immortal (it describes VtM \u201cstandard\u201d setting too), I prefer to be one of few heroes fighting overpowered monsters.<br /> <br /> I am not questioning your game, I just want to say that if he wants to play Scion where the gods don\u2019t changed the world, or where people don\u2019t care about the gods, it\u2019s up to him and the other players.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-18T08:59:19-07:00","id":1397303,"title":"","content":"Anyway, I can\u2019t wait till this book is available on DTRPG. The Setting Dials idea really does sound pretty awesome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-18T10:03:05-07:00","id":1397320,"title":"","content":"<i>Other people working on their iron dial setting for scion.<br /> <br /> Me : </i>&quot;Hm, i wonder what would happen if i cram every dials to gold ... and then push the dials further.&quot; XD","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-18T10:39:16-07:00","id":1397325,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11312_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11312\" data-vbnamecard=\"11312\">Maitrecorbo</a> \ud83d\ude02\ud83d\ude02\ud83d\ude02<br /> <br /> I think Bronze sounds ideal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-18T11:57:08-07:00","id":1397341,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1395335-companion-theocentrism-evidance-dials?p=1397283#post1397283\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I honestly don\u2019t see any fun on a game where your character is no more than a peon in a game of ancient Immortal (it describes VtM \u201cstandard\u201d setting too), I prefer to be one of few heroes fighting overpowered monsters.<br /> <br /> I am not questioning your game, I just want to say that if he wants to play Scion where the gods don\u2019t changed the world, or where people don\u2019t care about the gods, it\u2019s up to him and the other players.</div> </div> </div> </div>What a depressing outlook. There being OTHER Heroes doesn't make you're any less important. Do you think that the people who you saved from the giant wolf will react with a &quot;Y'know it would have been cooler if that Scion of Indra had saved us&quot;?<br /> <br /> Did people in myth ever go &quot;PERSEUS? Ugh, he's trash tier. Should have been Hercules.&quot;<br /> <br /> The Gods being real and this being known shouldn't make what your Heroes do irrelevant assuming you have a halfway competent GM. <i>A PC should never be framed as being a Peon or irrelevant in Scion, and any GM who does that is not doing a good job</i>. They should always be a Protagonist in their own stories.<br /> <br /> If you have the Gods, by existing, overshadow your PCs,then I'm going to go against my own signature and say <i>you're doing it wrong</i>. And if some smart-alec player goes &quot;Wait why doesn't [God] do something about this problem we're facing?&quot; just look them right in the eyes and say &quot;They sent <i>you</i>&quot;<br /> <br /> Now the number of Scions is up to tones with your games. I personally go with &quot;Enough&quot;.<br /> <br /> &quot;How many Heroes are there in the World?&quot; &quot;Enough.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;How many is that?&quot; &quot;<i>Enough</i> for my story.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;What's the number?&quot; &quot;It doesn't matter. There's enough for my story. No more, no less. If I need the PCs to meet another NPC Hero then they meet one. I'm not putting a number down because it's literally pointless. The number is Enough. Not so many that literally the entire World is Heroes, but not so few that they never encounter one-another.&quot;<br /> <br /> And as for the Gods struggling with lack of faith... The heck does lack of belief have to do with anything? Belief doesn't power Gods in most religions. They simply ARE. If people stopped worshipping Durga today, Durga would keep on keeping on and maintaining the universe. If people stopped invoking Zeus's name, Zeus would still exist. If people stopped making offerings to the Teotl... Well that'd be bad but not because they need FAITH, they need those offerings to keep the world working and the sun lit, but that's not powering them by belief.<br /> <br /> So yeah, in my opinion comparing &quot;The Gods are real and you're their champions and this is a Known Thing&quot; to &quot;You the player are a Peon&quot; is at best <i>grossly</i> reductionist and in very bad faith.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-18T12:41:28-07:00","id":1397352,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2142_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2142\" data-vbnamecard=\"2142\">Kyman201</a> I agree with you on this point. I don\u2019t see Scions as \u201cpeons.\u201d","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-19T22:14:04-07:00","id":1397624,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maitrecorbo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1395335-companion-theocentrism-evidance-dials?p=1397320#post1397320\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Other people working on their iron dial setting for scion.<br /> <br /> Me : </i>&quot;Hm, i wonder what would happen if i cram every dials to gold ... and then push the dials further.&quot; XD</div> </div> </div> </div>I honestly have this impulse to try to work out what every single dial combination would look like as a setting.<br /> <br /> I really do wonder what would be the most interesting version of &quot;everything is Iron except for X which is Gold?&quot;, because I am weird.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-20T17:12:57-07:00","id":1397848,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1395335-companion-theocentrism-evidance-dials?p=1397624#post1397624\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I honestly have this impulse to try to work out what every single dial combination would look like as a setting.<br /> <br /> I really do wonder what would be the most interesting version of &quot;everything is Iron except for X which is Gold?&quot;, because I am weird.</div> </div> </div> </div>Set the Evidence to Gold and everything else to Iron. Everything's low key, subdued, but everybody fucking knows that Gods exist<br /> <br /> Edit: Okay, this works a bit better with some than others. And keep in mind as three of these assume Iron Theocentrism (and I'm deliberately ignoring the &quot;I guess if you want this can also be set to Gods Barely Exist&quot; lines) then your tone may change mildly depending on which Cosmology you favor.<br /> <br /> <b>Gold Genre, Iron Otherwise</b>: I hope you're ready for the adventures of JACK HEROMAN! With Genre set to gold, everything is bonkers and over the top, Scale is fucking everywhere, explosions, thwarting the nefarious Baron Blade and his Blade Battalion! And he's gotta face down other bad guys, since the Titanomachy Iron means that if there were any Titan threat it was a long time ago. But due to the Theocentrism dial set down he only has one Divine Patron, and with Evidence set to Iron nobody has any idea that Jack Heroman is actually Chosen of Thor, nor can anybody prove it.<br /> <br /> <b>Gold Theocentrism, Iron Otherwise</b>: Things are super low-key and subtle. Faith and the Gods are everywhere, however. The Durga Puja is celebrated worldwide every year, people hold feasts in honor of Zeus, and the Gods listen, but work in mysterious ways. That's good, as with Iron Titanomachy, the Enemies of the Gods have left the mortal World mostly ignored. This setting is actually pretty good for below-deck type adventures.<br /> <br /> <b>Gold Titanomachy, Iron Otherwise</b>: Okay this one's gonna be a bit of an OOF. Well the good news is that due to the Iron Theocentrism, it's only ONE Pantheon's enemies terrorizing the World. This setting is probably the most dependent on which Pantheon you're favoring. Let's go with the Teotl, because they're more obvious and I haven't used them yet. So, the sun is... Darker than it was. While the Star Demons now only rarely descend from the heavens at night to steal people under the stars to devour, everyone has heard of someone who knows someone whose cousin vanished when the sun set. Your players will slowly uncover the truth of the World, about the monsters that rule it, and work covertly to sabotage them.<br /> <br /> <b>Gold Evidence, Iron Otherwise</b>: There's one Pantheon, everybody knows about it. You work at an insurance claims department, investigating whether it was <i>actually</i> Sun Wukong who smashed through a bus or if it just fell off a cliff and thus wouldn't be covered under Act Of Actual Gods claims. The game ends with the party actually getting jobs cataloging the antics of the Shen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":2142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","user":"Kyman201","date":". 06-21-2020, 01:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-21T08:28:53-07:00","id":1397989,"title":"","content":"Thanks. Is it weird that I find all of those to sound potentially fun?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-21T09:55:39-07:00","id":1398000,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1395335-companion-theocentrism-evidance-dials?p=1397989#post1397989\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks. Is it weird that I find all of those to sound potentially fun?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well I was trying to jazz them up so i'll take that as a compliment towards my ability to do elevator pitches","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-21T13:10:37-07:00","id":1398046,"title":"","content":"I think it would actually be an interesting idea for a Nexus project, just an overview of the dial combinations and what they might mean, including pantheon variations and mixes for when theocentrism is at Iron/Heroic or Bronze.<br /> <br /> It also occurs to me that having Theocentrism at, say, Heroic or Bronze and Evidence at Silver or Gold might result in some fun alternate history/fantasy settings. Like if your only pantheons are the Theoi and Shen, and it looks like a slightly more modern version of the novel Celestial Matters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-04T22:19:12-07:00","id":1401059,"title":"","content":"Netflix <b><i>Ragnarok </i></b>TV series is a story about two brothers coming back in their high school years to their hometown in Norwegian mountains. They do not know that town is ruled by the Giants \u2013 and they are reincarnations of the Aesir Gods themselves.<br /> Series is playing very much as <b>Scion: Origin</b> tier story, where everything start very mortal like. However, unlike the standard <b>Scion </b>setting, Gods and Giants are \u2018in hiding\u2019, covered by some kind of mystical mists.<br /> <br /> This series is everything I would do with <b>Scion</b> game on my own! \u2764\ufe0f Whole topic on forum we have <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1401051-netflix-ragnarok-tv-series-as-scion-chronicle\">here</a>.<br /> <br /> Official trailer<br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=7H9AaiBLHCo\" data-code=\"7H9AaiBLHCo\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/7H9AaiBLHCo/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-10T00:53:31-07:00","id":1402021,"title":"","content":"I personally would almost always want high mythology levels. If I want a game about hidden mythological creatures in the 'mists' I'm play channeling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/706-rickayelm","name":"rickayelm","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"76"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-14T23:16:14-07:00","id":1408317,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/315311/Mysteries-of-the-World-The-Scion-Second-Edition-Companion\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Scion 2E Companion</b></a> book is in the public sales - <b>So what are your Dials plans, especially on Theocentrism and Evidence fields?</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-15T00:10:26-07:00","id":1408320,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1395335-companion-theocentrism-evidance-dials?p=1408317#post1408317\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/315311/Mysteries-of-the-World-The-Scion-Second-Edition-Companion\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Scion 2E Companion</b></a> book is in the public sales - <b>So what are your Dials plans, especially on Theocentrism and Evidence fields?</b></div> </div> </div> </div>To quote myself from another thread: The absolute last thing I think when I crack open a book about Gods, Myth, Legend, and Heroes is &quot;Boy howdy I can't wait to absolutely minimize all the cool stuff&quot;. Theocentrism Gold in basically everything in all my games. Even in games where I plan on having the return of a Mythic cycle or something, where the Gods have been gone for a while but are returning, I'm gonna have all the Pantheons I feel like.<br /> <br /> Evidence will vary. Most of them I'll go with pretty high, but I had a vague idea for a Shadowrun-adjacent Cyberpunk-ish setting, where the Evidence would start low... But not because there's an active masquerade or because the Gods are trying to be low-key, but because they've been Away for a while. Hard to get evidence when Heroes have only been back for a bit and the PCs are the first Heroes in a while.<br /> <br /> And even then, most Denizens still exist and are out and about.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-15T00:50:19-07:00","id":1408321,"title":"","content":"One idea I\u2019ve had would be to have one dial be iron, but everything else be gold. Like for example Iron Theocentrism but everything else gold? Well then with gold Titanomachy the Asuras are invading in full force, but do not fear as the Deva\u2019s avatars and Scions are here in their myriad forms to fight and protect the World. With gold genre action is everywhere, Scions will be fighting Asuras all the time who seek to conquer all, with gold Evidence everyone is fully aware of the gods and their Scions are granted tons of leeway and gratitude and also plenty of space to use their Astras without fear","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24769-magicjohnny","name":"Magicjohnny","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24769_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-15T12:24:31-07:00","id":1408395,"title":"","content":"I've never been tempted to alter the basic &quot;all myths are true&quot; of Theocentrism, but my first series was set in Hong Kong, and was effectively Iron Theocentric for the Shen. Theoretically, all the other pantheons existed, but they never made an appearance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24028-mike-mccall","name":"Mike McCall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24028_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"55"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-15T13:14:31-07:00","id":1408401,"title":"","content":"Oh yeah, even if I focused on one Pantheon on-screen at the time, the implication will be that the other Pantheons in most of my games exist, we're just not focusing on them right now.<br /> <br /> Like, there's a difference between &quot;How many Pantheons exist total&quot; and &quot;How many Pantheons are going to be the focus&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-15T13:25:08-07:00","id":1408405,"title":"","content":"Though in practice, that's not much of a difference. Something like <b>Scion: Ragnarok</b> isn't going to change much between the Aesir being the only Pantheon that exists vs. the Aesir being the only Pantheon that matters. And in my view, that's what you get when you turn the Theocentrism down to Iron.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-17T15:08:18-07:00","id":1408794,"title":"","content":"I kind of want to experiment with Theocentrism at a medium level and Evidence at mid to high, for some sort of weird alternate history fantasy thing. Say, for example, something where the Theoi and the Shen are the two dominant Pantheons, and most of Eurasia has been split for a millennia between Alexander's empire and the Han dynasty (or successor states), with perhaps a few others as outliers. Or an alternate northeastern North America split between followers of the Manitou and an Aesir Vineland that never went away. Though this is more likely to just be a creative thought exercise rather than something I'd actually run.<br /> <br /> I also want to figure out how to do something akin to Percy Jackson, but with all or most of the Pantheons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-17T19:29:45-07:00","id":1408833,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1395335-companion-theocentrism-evidance-dials?p=1408794#post1408794\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also want to figure out how to do something akin to Percy Jackson, but with all or most of the Pantheons.</div> </div> </div> </div>Never watched or read the Jackson books itself - but from the blurbs and some online reviews, I assume my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1275725-2e-setting-hack-gods-in-hiding-and-new-mythic-age?p=1310158#post1310158\"><b>Gods in Hidden Hack</b></a> ( i.e. Iron or Heroic Theocentrism and Evidence ) using idea of Mythical Mists should be solution. I was pointed that something like Mists are thing in Jackson series. Hack makes number of Pantheons in play irrelevant, as Mists are covering everything mythical - so you do not have all the 'we cannot have more Gods in this situation or it will be absurd'. Or, at least, dissonance is MUCH lower. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 08-18-2020, 08:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-17T19:46:54-07:00","id":1408835,"title":"","content":"Percy Jackson universe has all the pantheons, but their interaction is limited by the Mist in a certain way. The gods know about and probably can interact with other pantheons, but each pantheon have its own rules to manifest (the Theoi have avatars And god forms that kill on sight, while Netjer occupy the body of people to manifest in the world, having hosts and not kids).<br /> <br /> I would say it\u2019s Heroic in most aspects, maybe with iron evidence and a flexible Titanomachia (the titans are acting against Theoi, and Apophis is moving against Ra, and the Ragnarok is on the way, but on different level for each pantheon). On the books it\u2019s described that mortals can\u2019t see the true form of mythical stuff, but the demigods cant too, and the monster and relics may appear mundane even to them (the only non god that can see everything is the Oracle).<br /> <br /> Another thing is, different Mantles are like multiple personalities that manifest according to the presence around them. When Greeks and roman demigods are around the gods get weird, not knowing how to manifest properly, for example, at same time, Zeus had a daughter and Jupiter had a son with the same woman, what makes everything a bit more crazy...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":24985,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","user":"Mateus Luz","date":". 08-18-2020, 08:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-16T00:57:08-07:00","id":1448664,"title":"","content":"Great discussion from <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/543-professor-phobos\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"543\" data-vbnamecard=\"543\">Professor Phobos</a> about<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1448603-how-masquerade-is-kept-in-wtf?p=1448619#post1448619\"> 'Masquerade' in <b>Werewolf: the Forsaken</b></a>, but it can easily be translated to <b>Scion</b> World. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Idea of Sub-Dials is already part of <b>Mysteries of the World</b>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}